# fullrust support for tokio 1.53.1 — route target_os = "fullrust" through
# tokio's own Unix/Linux code, so feature "full" builds and works: net (TCP,
# UDP, AsyncFd, net::unix incl. UnixStream/Listener/Datagram, peer_cred,
# abstract names, unix::pipe), process (pidfd reaper + SIGCHLD orphan/signal
# reaper, piped stdio, kill_on_drop), signal (unix::signal, ctrl_c), fs Unix
# extensions (mode, custom_flags, DirEntry::ino, symlink, ...).
# Applied on top of crates.io tokio 1.53.1 (vendored in crates/tokio/).
#
# * Every cfg predicate in src/ (outside the io-uring-only files) rewritten by
#   ../patches/fullrust-cfg.py --keep tokio_unstable:
#     unix               -> any(unix, target_os = "fullrust")
#     target_os="linux"  -> any(target_os = "linux", target_os = "fullrust")
#   (also inside tokio's `feature! { #![..] }`). `all(..)` groups naming
#   tokio_unstable (io-uring, taskdump: their deps are Linux-only) are left
#   alone. fullrust std provides std::os::unix / std::os::linux, so the
#   upstream Unix code compiles as is.
# * New file src/fullrust_libc.rs: a private stand-in for the libc items the
#   Linux paths use (Linux x86-64 layouts/values, raw `syscall`s) and for the
#   two signal-hook-registry items tokio uses (`register`, `FORBIDDEN`):
#   rt_sigaction with an sa_restorer trampoline, SA_RESTART|SA_SIGINFO,
#   actions run in registration order, previous handler chained. The
#   signal-hook-registry crate is not used: it is a cfg(unix) dependency whose
#   own `libc` calls (sigaction) would need a fork of its own.
# * Hand edits: `mod fullrust_libc` + a `last_os_error!` macro (lib.rs; it is
#   `io::Error::last_os_error()` on other targets, the shim's errno on
#   fullrust, which has no C errno), `use crate::fullrust_libc as libc` in the
#   8 files that name libc (with `signal_hook_registry` in signal/unix.rs),
#   `last_os_error!()` at the 9 libc error sites, and an explicit 0 third
#   argument at the 3 two-argument `fcntl(fd, F_GETFL)` calls (libc's fcntl
#   is variadic; identical on every target).
# * Cargo.toml: check-cfg for target_os = "fullrust". tokio's cfg(unix)
#   dependencies (libc, signal-hook-registry) stay out of the build graph.

